OL,3,ASummer 2026 expected to be declared
OL,4,AUK's hottest on record
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe Met Office is expected to confirm
OL,7,Fthat the UK has had its hottest summer
OL,8,Fsince records began in 1884.
OL,10,FProvisional figures for the months of
OL,11,FJune, July and August are due to be
OL,12,Freleased on Tuesday afternoon and are
OL,13,Flikely to reveal that mean temperatures
OL,14,F- which include daytime and overnight
OL,15,Fvalues - have broken the previous
OL,16,Frecord, set just last year.
OL,18,FIt follows a spring and summer of
OL,19,Fpersistent heat with five widespread
OL,20,Fheatwaves and 40 days of temperatures
OL,21,Fabove 30C (86F), smashing the previous
OL,22,Frecord of 34 days.
OL,23,APub: 31-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
